In this discussion, James sought guidance on modifying a `ggplot` command to separate "Costs" bars from other stacked categories, specifically to have the "Costs" appear alongside stacked "Climate" and "Pollution" bars. I initially suggested using `position_dodge()` in conjunction with a new variable, `stack_group`, to distinguish "Costs" from other categories. Upon further clarification, I adjusted the approach to filter the data between stacked and dodged bars. Despite these adjustments, James continued to encounter issues with the "Costs" not properly dodging while other bars were stacked. The final suggestion involved using separate `geom_col_pattern()` calls for stacking and dodging with appropriate data filtering, while retaining the dodge's effectiveness.
